	"nodes":[
		{"id":"f76697419cd567c3","type":"text","text":"lowk tho it would make sense for the game to take a set amount of time (maybe like 3-4 months?). Don't let the game end too early.","x":140,"y":-1300,"width":250,"height":140,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ca026a6c5d65d409","type":"text","text":"# Game Beats brainstorming\n---\n### Beginning:\n--- \n* Game starts in a Rakugo Hall. Shinigami kun is telling the story, as a jellyfish. Disclaimer that everyone is a jellyfish before he becomes his Gijinka form.\n\t* Do a Rakugo bit before bowing and moving onto the next scene\n\t\n* (March 31st) Meet Shinki, a jellyfish girl recently kicked out of her house for being framed for embezzlement. She's at her lowest point, but the closer she's pushed to death the more determined she is to make money\n* Meet Shinigami kun, who wants to torment her but is fascinated by her business proposal, and agrees. Possesses Shinki.\n\n* Start quack doctor scheme (Shinki: \"If it works, is it really a scam?\")\n\t* Tutorial for quack doctor scheme. Will be used in the management sim aspect\n\t* You go into the house, see the patient in their futon. \n\t* Shinigami kun will be at the foot of the bed (ik it might not be accurate to the story but for game reasons I really want it to work like this.)\n\n### Management Sim part\n--- \n* Rounds span a week. Each round has x turns.\n    *  General Round things:\n    \t* Beginning of Round: Advertise, Customize office, Go Shopping\n\t    \t* *(Allow player to choose prices after the first round?)*\n\t\t    \t* Or even better, allow players to choose what kind of fees to tack on (each fee lowers the chance of success)\n        \t* Certain items make the game easier, boost your chances of feet shinigami, or are just requests from Shinigami kun\n\t        \t* Money Omamori: 500 yen\n        * Middle of Round: Go to different places, heal or refuse.\n        * End of Round: Hang out with Shinigami kun (Affection meter maybe? Or satisfaction meter ig. This is required or else he will leave. Maybe). Some events require money\n        * You can only choose up to 5 clients per round. You can choose them from a pool of 10 though\n\t        * Maybe there's an item that lets you choose up to 7 per round? (or maybe that's just the advertising)\n    * Nozaki Family are a forced event and will come depending on your money threshold during a round, or will come when you buy a certain item\n\t    * OR, maybe they'll just show up on your list in the 4th week and you can just completely skip them if you want. But maybe they'll pay like, a lot of money or they'll offer the player something super valuable in return\n\t\t    * Or maybe Shinki will mention that they own a shrine when she pulls up the phone and Shinigami kun will be like \"Ugh, those places ick me out. Maybe you should avoid them.\"\n\t\t    * Another Idea:\n\t\t\t    * They give you a little talisman that lets you drive any Shinigami kun out temporarily, as a free gift for every route (discretely, without him knowing). \n\t\t\t    * You can use it on a failed exorcism, but you should save it for the Hiue family(?) (atp i think that's too many moving parts tho)\n    *  Have a vitality meter? \n\t    * Round ends when you run out. After each round you start with less and less of it.\n\t\t    * Make this look vaguely like a candle. But not so much that it's obvious to players. It'll be like a generic energy bar thing\n\t\t\t    * Maybe when it goes down it'll look like melting\n\t\t    * Taking jobs makes it go lower by a set amount.\n\t\t    * Hanging out with Shinigami kun also makes it lower by a set amount (albeit smaller. He *is* a shinigami, after all. Even if he isn't actively killing you)\n\t    * The more jobs you take, the less vitality you have in the next round\n\t\t    * I wonder why...\n\t* Exorcism part\n\t\t* Maybe it'll be like undertale where you just have to hit the target\n\t\t\t* The bonuses you buy can make this easier or harder, but at some point you'll just be fighting against chance \n\t\t\t\t* Wait... this is not a bad idea. Have a secret value hidden from the player. \n\t\t\t\t* Have the spell\n\t\t\t* \n\t\t* Or we can just take out skill entirely and just have the player look for the shinigami with shinigami eyes(?)\n\t\t\t* Ofc we can hear a clip of someone saying the spell and allow the player to hit a button to emulate clapping\n* Hiue Family    \n\t* Fatal disease in the balls. I'm joking that it's caused by Shinigami kun but he did really want it to happen.\n    * Shinigami kun wants to go only so he can be the one to do his brother in. \n    * Shinki goes, but then decides to work with Jirou and tricks Shinigami kun- (who gets driven away maybe).\n\t    * Time skip, after a while the amount of headside shinigami increases and Shinki can't make money anymore, she's desperate. \n\t\t    * Takes the Hiue job. Shinigami kun just wants to do him in.\n\t\t\t    * He knows he'll be caught here, but he just wants revenge. Jirou was fated to die early, anyways. \n\t\t    * Jirou's second wife is on the bedside. Shinki gets promised funding for a business deal if she can at least save his life for a little longer.. She can't refuse. \n\t\t    * She remembers the spell the Nozakis taught her to rid herself of Shinigami kun. She does that, and Shinigami kun is driven out\n\t\t\t    * Or actually it's just the same spell and Shinki gets a relic that makes it work on Shinigami kun.\n\t\t    * Shinigami kun is... driven out. (side)\n\t\t    * She gets the deal, leaves, and finds Shinigami kun waiting out front. \"You think that cheap piece of fabric could do me in for good? God, you're so stupid\"\n\t\t    * Grabs her by the wrist, and brings her down to his secret little cave, with a single candle. \n\t\t\t    * Grabs Shinki's candle from her heart.\n\t    * Idk, maybe if you go bankrupt before the 5th month, you're forced to take the Hiue family job and that leads to the worst ending(?)\n\t\t    * If you're forced to take the Hiue job, then the ending changes depending on when you go bankrupt\n\t\t\t    * 1st week: Worst ending. Shinigami kun blows out the candle for you. Shinigami kun also won't say much about Jirou other than that he hates him.\n\t\t\t    * 2nd week: \n\t\t* \n    * She gets thanked, etc etc, and then when she leaves the building she sees Shinigami kun waiting outside\n    * Gets dragged out to the underworld and sees the candles. See [[The Shinigami that is also a Jellyfish#Endings (most result in you becoming a shinigami)|Endings]]\n- List of rounds: \n\t- Round 1: \n\t\t- Right after Shinki finishes the tutorial. She doesn't have enough money for an apartment so she lives in a net cafe for the time being  \n\t\t- Lowk this is a good time for a general game tutorial since there isn't much to do other than make money (general idea of how the menus work) \n- Numbers by round\n\n| Round |     | Payment* | Available Events                                                                  | Special Items to Buy                                                                                                                                      |\n| ----- | --- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 1     |     | 5-10k    | <br>- Read Manga<br>- Conbini run<br>- Surf the web<br>- Play in the park<br>     | - New clothes (for Shinigami san): 4.5k<br>   - They make him happier ig<br>- New clothes (for Shinki): 3.5k<br>   - (they give you a 1k boost in profit) |\n| 2     |     | 10-15k   |                                                                                   | - Apartment                                                                                                                                               |\n| 3     |     | 10-17k   | - \"Please give me your customer service smile\"<br>   - Player can choose yes / no |                                                                                                                                                           |\n| 4     |     | 15-20k   |                                                                                   |                                                                                                                                                           |\n| 5     |     | 15-30k   |                                                                                   |                                                                                                                                                           |\n*\\*Anything above the cap will be a guaranteed fail*\n\n### Endings (most result in you dying):\n--- \n* **Love ending**: Maybe kinda yandere? Not sure. \n\t* If you do a certain amount of events. Shinki becomes his raison d'ete, but after the betrayal he decides that he'll just keep her here. Forever.\n* **Candle endings**: Have the candle scene. Hold the candle with the mouse and wait until its lit fully. \n\t* If the player moves the candle before it's //fully// lit, she will die. Shinigami kun will talk while this happens so if the player moves mouse to move along with his dialogue, they die (\"Haha. You think you could light anything with those shakey hands?\"). You just have to hold still and let him talk. (God. This is peak role embodiment tho, You have to ignore him)\n\t\t* Note: Maybe have the candle shake a little by itself and you have to fangangle against it? I like that better lowk\n\t\t* The shinigami will still talk but if you don't fanangle against Shinki's hands while you read then you die\n    * If player lights the candle\n    \t* 1% chance she sneezes and blows it out (get fucked lol) (rolls each time the scene is loaded for the completionists)\n        * Otherwise, Shinigami kun just claps and disappears- ending the interaction and friendship coldly.\n        * Then Shinki goes home as if nothing ever happend...\n        \t* Actually, when Shinki goes to sleep, she sees him by the head of her futon. \"Shit\"\n            * If you didn't buy ofuda (very hard, you need to make a lot of money and fight Shinki on the menuing), the game ends there. Otherwise, you slap the ofuda on him and uh, it gives you enough time to escape. \n            * The win is empty though, and you're back to square one. Now with a shinigami on your heels. Escape the country and change your name.\n","x":-760,"y":-1860,"width":1320,"height":2600},
		{"id":"9e4fd76649f01d32","type":"text","text":"\n# Lore Notes:\n--- \nShinigami kun\n* Prefers his new life as a Shinigami. \n\t* He likes the feeling of being untouchable and having the freedom to do whatever he wants\n* Prized possession is the letter Saburou wrote to him before death. He doesn't have it anymore, but he has at least half of it memorized.\n* Can eat, but only when offered food through people who have a connection with him (can't have him be too ghost-ly now. He must still be bound by the rules of death)\n\t* Could be a good view into what dead people are like in Ite, since we have two ghosts. Nozaki-chan would prolly be able to bend the rules thanks to her lineage tho\n* Super squeamish about copepods, crabs, and the like. Almost pathetically so.\n\n\nShinigami Lore\n* Not psychopomps (?), makes the candle thing kinda obselete\n\t* Though Shinigami nowadays are understood to be grim reapers\n* Cave of candles \n\t* Tbh this part isn't particularly Japanese, since it was imported from a western story. Struggling to incorporate it into the story. I'm thinking it's something specific to the Hiue family tho (like flame rising)\n\t\t* Maybe it can be like a thing in the underworld\n\t\t* The Hiues are in charge of it, of course (hiue = rising flame)\n\t* Maybe it has something to do with the family Kami (jellyfish hero or smth idk. Managed to strike down a turtle all on her lonesome with such speed she caught on ocean fire. Jellyfish Fireball much?)\n\t\t* Pities her descendants and the awful tradition, but feels its necessary because weak jellyfish can't protect shit.\n\t\t\t* Many turn into youkai because of it, and she has the ones that *can* pass on hunt them down so they don't cause harm to future descendants or other Jellyfish (which she will not tolerate)\n\t\t\t* Maybe Shinigami kun possesses Shinki so that he can escape them? \n\t\t\t\t* He's different from other Shinigami, who kill because it's the life order. He's specifically a renegade shinigami. \n\t\t\t\t* WAIIIIT What if he originally pretended he passed peacefully to get access to the candle, and stole Jirou's candle. He had to leave it somewhere because he ran away from the other shinigamis under the grand Hiue. That's where he takes Shinki when she betrays him\n\t\t\t\t\t* Couldn't Shinigami kun have just blew out Jirou's candle(?) (No, I want him to see my face as he dies). He's in this for spiteful revenge\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* Also lowk maybe candles are tied to the person they're for, so Shinigami kun can take it out if Shinki for the scene. \n\t\t\t\t* Jirou falls into a coma, so his candlelight goes out momentarily. At this point, his life is up to Shinki and Shinigami kun- not fate.\n\t\t\t\t* Chose Shinki because when he possessed her, her drive to make money won over her drive to die\n\t\t\t\t\t* So it's kinda like, mutual I guess? Shinigami kun needs her to be alive to hide, and Shinki needs to make money for her goals and also so she doesn't succumb to shinigami things\n\t\t\t\t* Chose Shinki because he could see her candle was going to go out relatively soon (but not so soon that he wouldn't have a chance to kill Jirou)\n\t\t\t\t\t* Convenience! Also she was funny.\n\t\t\t\t\t* ALSO, that would mean he really wants to save her. Though uh, why didn't he just tell her everything before she acted herself? \n\t\t\t\t\t\t* Shinki fatal flaw: Blinded by money. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t* Shinigami kun: Tells her that Jirou is his brother and that he wants to replace his candle with hers. So no matter what, do not heal him. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* What if he just tells her to not heal Jirou no matter what, and not about the candle thing? (It's about trust baybee, that makes the betrayal hurt more ^-^)\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* Either way is a win-win for him. Shinigami kun is a very spiteful jelly\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* If Shinki manages to light it: He'll follow her and kill her spitefully.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* Also either way Shinki lowk made bad blood with the Hiue family, she's gonna change her name and run away anyways(?)\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* If Shinki blows it out: He'll just snuff Jirou's candle next\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t* Lowk ig this means Katsuo is raised by his bio mother since his dad is definitely not making out of this one alive.\n\t\t\t\t* Either that or I scrap the tsukimono kill thing and Shinigami just possesses her because she's convenient and interesting. (it's ok to do this btw, it happens in the rakugo)\n\t\t* Maybe the Hiues as Shinigami are fucking terrifying? Like king of the hill kinda terrifying (nah, continuity issues)\n\t\t\t* (But then why can't he just drive all the shinigami away?)\n\t\t\t\t* Balance thing? \n\t\t\t* What happened to the other Hiues?\n\t\t\t\t* They all passed on, I think. \n\t\t\t* Past hiues definitely can't mess with hiues that are alive. That defeats the whole purpose of the tradition\n* Maybe he died in a way that made him into a shinigami, rather than allowing him to pass on (nah, the ancestor  idea is better)\n\t* tbf i'm sure the other siblings also passed in traumatic ways. \n\t\t* Candle candle candle \n\t* ... bro i'm already back to square one lol. This was the idea before ??? \n\t\t* It just has to be way worse than how his siblings died\n\t\t* Jiro killed him but also tormented him because they had reaaally bad blood.\n\t\t\t* Destroyed his letter in a fire in front of him? \n\t\t\t\t* Incinerated? (Hiues that die this way get a special )\n\t\t\t* Electricity?\n\t\t\t* Firing squad (boring)\n\t\t\t* Lethal injection?\n\t\t\t* Pinned him to the wall with nails and shot/sliced\n\t\t\t* Boiled alive?\n\t\t* Locked/locked in a room and eaten alive by parasites (... 👀). Maybe it's one of Futao's special torture methods that he wanted to test out lowk. Reason why he finds Shinki is because he has vertical migration unlocked\n\t\t\t* Jirou went to such lengths Futao suggested it on a whim. He thinks it's fitting because Shirou fucked around a lot and he has no respect for him.\n\t\t\t* wait holy shit kuru kuru kurikaesu (Shirou learns that they both turn on him, he tries to escape but instead gets lost in the underbelly of the governmental structure)\n\t\t\t\t* The test subjects are like 3 years old atp. I could maybe foreshadow them\n\t\t\t* This is just giving a cruel game of cat and mouse. \n* ","x":660,"y":-1860,"width":920,"height":1720},
		{"id":"93d762e046b5f08b","type":"text","text":"Inspo Pics","x":-2060,"y":-2440,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"f2cbc1e2c7bb7986","type":"file","file":"Images/Pasted image 20260222204906.png","x":-2300,"y":-2340,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"8929f0ea1f571fbc","type":"text","text":"# Ailments\n- Parasites, physical damage\n\t- Hole/ rips in bell, tentacles, broken \n\t- Apparently bacteria can eat holes or disintegrate (moon) jellyfish within 48 hours\n- Poison\n\t- coral/anemone/bigger jellyfish poison (Shinigami kun can relate)\n\t- Heavy metal pollution\n- No explanation\n\t- Weakness (very little pulse)\n\t- Not eating\n- Eversion\n\t- Not a big issue since jellyfish are sapient, but it does render them unable to eat on their own\n- Balling (Inversion)\n\t- Caused by trauma, water chemistry, or improper water flow\n- Magnesium Chloride(?)\n\n[for more ideas on ailments](http://www.jellyfishcare.com/)\n\n[Jellyfish Care Handbook (AZA) Ch7 p39](https://assets.speakcdn.com/assets/2332/aza_jellyfish_care_manual.pdf)","x":380,"y":-3080,"width":318,"height":840},
		{"id":"f6ad27cd671b1c3e","type":"text","text":"# Ideas for Patients\n--- \n- First Client: \n\t- Super wealthy. Kinda an asshole. Maybe a pain in the ass in Ite lowk\n\t- \"I can't thank you enough. The gift of life you've given me is priceless\"\n\t- \"You can start by giving me money.\"\n\t- \"Ah... right, this should be enough...\" (gives her 30k)\n\t- *God, this jellyfish is definitely out of touch... I'll happily take the money though.*\n- Nozaki Family:\n\t- Maybe Yuune? Or maybe Shinigami kun just notices her in the corner and notes how something is off about her (atp she's very young).\n- Futao / Kazuo:\n\t- Fakeout cause lowk that's what did in the guy in the grimm's fairytale.\n- Hiue Family:\n\t- Jirou with the disease in his balls\n\t- Katsuo keeps floating over to him. lol.\n- Moon Jellyfish \n\t- Inverted bell\n\t- Rough shape\n\t- One of these is Sui maybe? \n- Red lantern jellyfish ?\n- Hanakari jellyfish ? (same genus, dif species as prev)\n- Urashima kurage (*urashimea globosa*)\n- Kami kurage (*Spirocodon salator*)\n- Yamaguchi (Shinigami kun has interesting dialog if you choose this one)\n\t- Teri has 2 older siblings, but he is 16 atp.\n\t- Oh lowk the light novel happens around this time. Maybe we can get some of Shima's art as an easter egg\n- Akakurage (*Chrysaora pacifica*)\n- *Mastigias papua*\n- Other *Cassiopea ornata*s\n- *Nemophilema nomurai*\n- Bizen Kurage (*Rhopilema esculentum*)\n- Ebikurage (*Netrostoma setouchiana*)\n- Murasaki Kurage (*Thysanostoma*)\n- Jellyfish from the Kyoto Suizokukan\n\t- Black Kurage\n\t- One of Achlys' godmothers(?) (ik they're *Chrysaora melanaster* but the point still stands)\n- Okikurage\n\t- One of Naito's older siblings? Maybe it gets her to start drawing because she's so sad\n- Andon kurage (*Carybdea brevipedalia*)\n- *Aequora sp* (There's many different species in Japan)\n- Hanagasa kurage\n\t- Taka Ryuu's Aunt\n\t- lowk imply that he was the one who killed her(?)\n\t- Anyways you can't heal her. \n- *Craspedacusta sowerbyi*\n\nNote: I wanna shoot for at least [x] amount of clients","x":-860,"y":-3120,"width":1200,"height":1160},
		{"id":"ba3c581d45a04c31","type":"text","text":"big cities tend to have dead zone issues unless they plant lots of algae and stuff","x":630,"y":-3136,"width":250,"height":112},
		{"id":"86f7ae42f42c0a6d","type":"text","text":"<iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/DjuvTwSipa8?si=8RpBQ0yyjeoASTKk\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>","x":-2549,"y":-1637,"width":614,"height":337},
		{"id":"c349fbfe287b3d8a","type":"text","text":"MUSIC","x":-2367,"y":-1800,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"5656eb2d68c6eecc","type":"text","text":"Jellyfish disease isn't well-studied in the present day. maybe the [[The Sakasai Family]] also does a lot of pharmaceutical stuff?\n\nShinki must feel pretty powerful healing ailments her family hasn't been able to heal.\n- (With the wave of a tentacle, I can do the work of god...)\nGranted she's just driving out shinigamis but shhh no one needs to know","x":747,"y":-2781,"width":250,"height":481},
		{"id":"24101d80085d6c6d","type":"text","text":"lowk not sure what century to make the game in\n\nwould it be cheating to just not put in the year...?","x":-1360,"y":-1780,"width":250,"height":160},
		{"id":"509bc734825350a4","type":"text","text":"Game starts on March 31st. Shinki graduated a [week prior](https://www.kyoto-u.ac.jp/en/current/campus-life/event/ceremony/graduation), but was given until March before she was forced to leave","x":-1360,"y":-1600,"width":250,"height":143},
		{"id":"100bf9b9b82992e4","type":"text","text":"Money\n--- \n### Net Cafe\nLowk the only realworld net cafe in Kyoto that offered a 1 week plan was CocoNe net cafe. 23,990 for the mat-type room \n![[Pasted image 20260221005250.png]]\nHer first client probably gave her like 25k lowk (truly a miracle cure)\n### Apartment\n18 sq meters and 18k per month\n\nhttps://rentola.com/listings/p50f00d\n\nI think we can haggle with the price though, and it doesn't have to be 100% accurate to real japan.\n\nThough tbh 18k per month is doable considering the nature of the pay. The downpayment is just the issue (maybe Shinki haggles it down to 45k because she's just that business oriented)","x":-1640,"y":-1360,"width":490,"height":560},
		{"id":"258601a040bb942c","type":"text","text":"# Payment\nShould be paid on avg like 25k per successful thing by the end of it.\n\nhttps://myoryuji.com/archives/29960 \n- (In Japanese) general guideline for how much harae cost. You can expect them to be 5-30k for something like healing)\n\t- Shinki isn't technically an exorcist but she'd definitely act like one\n\nhttps://alea.care/resources/cost-health-Japan: \n- cost of healthcare (i forgot why i needed this)","x":-1560,"y":-742,"width":410,"height":402},
		{"id":"193dce264222b80c","type":"text","text":"This is the exact kind of jazz fusion I need. (Ofc I wanna reference CASSIOPEA but this is another style to look at)","x":-2740,"y":-1500,"width":250,"height":168},
		{"id":"165c12e309eaf809","type":"text","text":"Achievements\n---\n- Cheapskate: Go through the whole game without buying new clothes\n- Net Cafe Enthusiast: Never move out of the net cafe\n\t- Get a net cafe ID card in the gallery\n- Classic Ending: Blow out the candle yourself\n- Shakey Hands: Snuff out the candle right after lighting it on fire\n- Poor Ending: Have Shinigami-kun blow out the candle himself\n- Winner of Capitalism: Have more than [x] yen in the bank\n- Forbidden Love: Make the Shinigami fall in love with you","x":-1450,"y":-280,"width":600,"height":446,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"a86cf5760688d096","type":"text","text":"<iframe width=\"300\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/OSYmTw6_bjc?si=bzEaeX2nW1Q8uWAE\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>","x":-1520,"y":-3244,"width":340,"height":249},
		{"id":"69f060b4811af31d","type":"text","text":"ik this is a trans allegory but the idea of killing your siblings is also still true for the Hiue sibs","x":-1220,"y":-3260,"width":250,"height":140},
		{"id":"daf33aa8500fdad3","type":"text","text":"<iframe width=\"300\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/qj1GooBp0ss?si=BzkNNXXanlHqGjMX\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>","x":-1371,"y":-2980,"width":351,"height":260},
		{"id":"fcc9b84db544abd5","type":"text","text":"Kuruouze,,, (+ shinigami kun)","x":-1560,"y":-2960,"width":260,"height":60},
		{"id":"725aea3cc1f67f0e","x":687,"y":-38,"width":593,"height":518,"type":"text","text":"Rakugo notes\n---\n- Man dies because switching the futon switched his life with the dying man's life.\n- The shinigami going \"Hora? Hora hora horaaaaa?\" while the man's candle is going out is very funny and I think I need to put that in \n- The meta is that feet = life, head = death\n- The candles are just a part of the meta. The story doesn't really explain where all the candles come from or where the shinigami takes the protag\n\t- Making the hikurages in charge of keeping track of lifespan would be cool ig. Maybe they make candles\n- Would make sense for chironex to be in charge of that since they have the highest kill count\n- \"I hope you sold your life for a good price.\""},
		{"id":"1fc043d9080ac846","x":1400,"y":160,"width":340,"height":80,"type":"text","text":"Shinki swaps her own lifespan with Jirou's?"},
		{"id":"411a9bcff9df7ffc","x":1420,"y":-171,"width":320,"height":231,"type":"text","text":"<iframe width=\"300\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/P4PCds4tlT4?si=WREJyKmAVBDLl1ZO&amp;start=174\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>"},
		{"id":"40e6c237fc0fcecb","x":1340,"y":361,"width":547,"height":239,"type":"text","text":"---\n\n---\nshinigami kun and exorcism\n---\n- He gives Shinki the ability to see Shinigami\n\t- there's a death note joke in here SOMEWHERE\n- "}
